// NEGATIVE TEST -- `try { ... }` does not exist.
//
// `try` is not a keyword, so it lexes as an identifier and `try { }` is parsed
// as a struct literal for a struct nobody declared. The diagnostic names the
// misreading rather than the missing feature, which is why this is pinned: it
// is the observable behaviour a user actually gets.
fn main() {
    try { }
}
